+          <p>ForkMesh handles zero-custody relay through the same split it uses across the product: desktop nodes keep real Git mirrors, while mainnodes coordinate discovery, relay tunnels, presence, account lookup, and clone routing.</p>
+          <p>The behavior is intentionally narrow: The mainnode coordinates discovery, presence, and routing with Cloudflare Durable Objects, but it stores no packfiles and no message bodies. Objects stream between peers; the relay just connects them. The Worker helps find and route a live host, but it is not canonical Git storage.</p>
